                "Failure Mode 1: Overfitting and Mode Collapse. During pre-training, models are exposed to trillions of diverse tokens across hundreds of domains. In SFT, the training dataset is thousands of times smaller (often only tens of thousands of examples) and frequently concentrated in narrow conversational styles. If fine-tuned for too many epochs or with an aggressive learning rate (such as lr > 2e-5 on full parameter tuning), the model experiences Mode Collapse: it forgets the rich long-tail knowledge learned during pre-training and collapses onto stereotypical, repetitive response templates (e.g. starting every single sentence with 'As an AI language model...').",
