                "To mitigate repetition loops during post-training inference, generation controllers implement Repetition and Frequency Penalties. The standard repetition penalty discount (introduced by Keskar et al.) penalizes logits for any token that has already appeared in the generated prefix. For any token w in the vocabulary, if w has already appeared in the generated context, its logit z_w is transformed: z'_w = z_w / theta (if z_w > 0) or z'_w = z_w * theta (if z_w < 0), where theta > 1.0 (typically 1.1 to 1.2). By discounting logits of previously generated words, the repetition loop is broken.",
